                <tr id="issuerow10050035" rel="10050035" data-issuekey="CR-41564" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    NIQ Activate
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CR-41564" href="https://adlm.nielseniq.com/jira/browse/CR-41564">CR-41564</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Unlimitail - Segmentation - expand the offline export to support larger shopper exports
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype">    Epic
</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                <span class=" jira-issue-status-lozenge aui-lozenge jira-issue-status-lozenge-default jira-issue-status-lozenge-new aui-lozenge-subtle jira-issue-status-lozenge-max-width-medium" data-tooltip="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" title="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" tabindex="0">Draft</span>    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">           High
    </td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Tal Martsiano Shkedi
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Neta Gefen-Shternberg
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Eran Center
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 09/Sep/2026 9:57 AM </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> 11/Sep/2026 5:13 PM </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 09/Sep/2026 10:15 AM </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CR-39951                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Background / Context<br/>
Segmentation Studio currently supports exporting shopper audiences through two export mechanisms: * *Online export* supports up to approximately {*}1 million shoppers for shopper IDs only or up to 50K for e{*}{*}nriched shopper export{*} due to the significantly larger data footprint and number of exported attributes<br/>
 * *Offline / integration export* supports up to{*}1 million shoppers{*}<br/>
<br/>
These limits were established due to existing platform performance and scalability constraints.<br/>
As NIQ Activate expands to support larger retailers and retail media players, current export limits no longer meet customer needs. For example: * *Unlimitail&#39;s Carrefour France* may require audience exports of approximately *13–14 million shoppers* in a single export.<br/>
 * Future deployments for *Carrefour Brazil* and *Carrefour Spain* may require exports that exceed current limits and potentially surpass {*}30 million shoppers{*}. Exact audience volumes require validation with Unlimitail.<br/>
<br/>
The current platform limitation creates a scalability gap that restricts audience activation opportunities for large enterprise retailers and retail media clients.<br/>
h3. Problem Statement<br/>
The existing offline export architecture cannot reliably process very large shopper segments. As a result: * Large audiences must be reduced, split, or cannot be exported.<br/>
 * Customer activation use cases are constrained.<br/>
 * Expansion into large-scale retailer ecosystems is limited.<br/>
 * Operational workarounds may be required for strategic customers.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business Need<br/>
To support enterprise-scale retail media and activation scenarios, the platform must scale audience export capabilities beyond current limitations and support exports of *30 million shoppers or more* through the {*}offline/integration export pathway{*}.<br/>
Online export scalability is not part of the initial scope but future architectural decisions should avoid preventing future online scale enhancements.<br/>
 <br/>
h1. Business Outcome / Value<br/>
h3. Business Value<br/>
 * Supports expansion into larger retailer ecosystems and higher-volume activation opportunities.<br/>
 * Improves platform competitiveness for enterprise-scale retail media customers.<br/>
 * Positions Activate to support future audience growth across global markets.<br/>
<br/>
*Timelines*<br/>
 * Unlimitail goes live in PI4. without this capability their ability to use Activate for targeting will be very limited.<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
h1. Acceptance Criteria<br/>
h2.  <br/>
 * <br/>
*Offline export supports segments of at least 30 million shoppers* without requiring manual audience splitting.<br/>
 * <br/>
{*}Exported data is complete and accurate{*}, with no loss or duplication of shopper records.<br/>
 * <br/>
*Export processing remains reliable and operationally supportable* at the target scale, including monitoring and error handling.<br/>
 * <br/>
{*}Existing offline export integrations remain compatible{*}, unless explicitly approved changes are communicated.<br/>
 * <br/>
*The solution can be extended to support larger audience sizes in the future* without requiring a fundamental redesign.<br/>
 * *Successfully validated with representative customer-sized datasets.*<br/>
 * Export processing time remains within agreed SLA of {*}[TO BE DEFINED]{*}.<br/>
 * No material degradation of Segmentation Studio platform performance during large export execution.<br/>
----<br/>
h1. In Scope<br/>
 * Offline / Integration export scalability improvements.<br/>
 * Architectural changes required to support 30M+ shopper exports.<br/>
 * Data processing optimization.<br/>
 * Storage and transfer optimization.<br/>
 * Validation using representative large-scale datasets.<br/>
<br/>
h1. Out of Scope<br/>
 * Online export scalability beyond current limits.<br/>
 * Increasing enriched shopper export limits.<br/>
 * Changes to audience creation or segmentation logic.<br/>
 * Changes to export file schema or business definitions unless separately approved.<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h1. Risks &amp; Dependencies<br/>
h2. Dependencies<br/>
 * Validation of expected shopper volumes for Carrefour Brazil and Carrefour Spain.<br/>
 * Infrastructure capacity and cost assessment.<br/>
<br/>
h2. Risks<br/>
||Risk||Impact||<br/>
|Timelines: go live of Unlimitail is PI4|May limit Unlimitail&#39;s ability to use the segmentation studio|<br/>
|Export architecture does not scale linearly to 30M+ records|May require significant redesign and increase delivery effort|<br/>
|Infrastructure cost increases due to large-volume processing|May impact operational budgets|<br/>
|Downstream systems cannot ingest larger files|End-to-end value not realized|<br/>
|Long-running export jobs affect overall platform performance|Customer experience degradation|<br/>
|Future markets require volumes greater than 30M shoppers|Additional scalability work may be required|<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
 
  </td>
