                <tr id="issuerow10002534" rel="10002534" data-issuekey="CR-40955" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    NIQ Activate
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CR-40955" href="https://adlm.nielseniq.com/jira/browse/CR-40955">CR-40955</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Placeholder: Unlimitail - Indexing requirements
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype">    Epic
</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                <span class=" jira-issue-status-lozenge aui-lozenge jira-issue-status-lozenge-default jira-issue-status-lozenge-new aui-lozenge-subtle jira-issue-status-lozenge-max-width-medium" data-tooltip="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" title="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" tabindex="0">Draft</span>    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">           High
    </td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Neta Gefen-Shternberg
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Eran Center
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Aug/2026 8:59 AM </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 27/Aug/2026 9:27 AM </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate">0</td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate">0</td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">            0%
    </td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      *1. Background*<br/>
 <br/>
Unlimitail uses shopper indexes to analyze campaigns in terms of the shopper profiles buying the CPG/brand/advertised products, and to identify which channels are over- or under-indexed for the advertised products relative to their share of the total market. Indexing serves two purposes: measuring campaign performance after the fact, and identifying gaps and opportunities before a campaign runs.<br/>
 <br/>
Three distinct index types were identified in their reporting deck. This epic captures the requirements to support them.<br/>
 <br/>
—<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
*2. Epic Statement*<br/>
 <br/>
Extend our indexing capabilities so Unlimitail can benchmark shopper and channel behavior against the {*}{{*}}category{{*}}{*}, not only the total retailer, across the KPIs that matter to them (% shoppers, % sales, % units, % trips). This lets them identify shopper-profile skews and channel over/under-indexing for advertised products both for post-campaign measurement and pre-campaign opportunity sizing.<br/>
 <br/>
—<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
*3. Index Types*<br/>
 *Shopper attribute distribution (e.g., age) in Brand/CPG vs. in a Category -Q4/26 dev* * Whether a brand over/under-indexes on a shopper attribute vs. the category<br/>
 * Enhancement to existing Shopper Appeal report | {*}{{*}}Phase 1 – PI4{{*}}{*} |<br/>
 * E.g. % of 25-35 aged  shoppers in dove vs. %25-35 aged shoppers in shampoo<br/>
 * This can be part of shopper appeal report with some changes required:<br/>
 ** selecting the KPI to index on- % shoppers/%sales/%unit sales/%trips. <br/>
 ** Select the comparison level (today only retailer, should support filtered scope).<br/>
<br/>
*Channel share-of-sales within CPG/Brand/SKU vs. channel share-of-sales within tota* * Whether a channel is over/under-indexed in the brand&#39;s sales<br/>
 * New report / redesign of shopper appeal<br/>
 *  Not for PI4-  if possible<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
*Brand share-of-sales within Channel/Format/Banner vs. brand share across total channels/formats/banners*<br/>
  * Whether a brand is over/under-represented in a specific channel |<br/>
 * New report / redesign of shopper appeal <br/>
 *  Not for PI4-  if possible<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
Eran&#39;s recommendation: start with Type 1, since it is an enhancement to an existing report and can ship in PI4. Types 2 and 3 require a report redesign and are recommended to wait.<br/>
 <br/>
—<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
 *Phase 1 – Shopper Appeal Report Enhancement HL requirements(Type 1)*<br/>
 <br/>
 *  Current state<br/>
The Shopper Appeal report already calculates a similar index, but only vs. total retailer, and only on $ sales.<br/>
 <br/>
 * Requirements<br/>
 ** REQ-1.1 - Category benchmark:** Add the ability to calculate the index vs. {*}{{*}}category{{*}}{*}, in addition to the existing total retailer benchmark. User should be able to select which benchmark to use<br/>
 ** REQ-1.2 - KPI selection:** Add the ability to choose which KPI drives the index calculation: % shoppers, % sales ($), % unit sales, or % trips. Today only $ sales is supported.<br/>
 ** REQ-1.3 - Independent configuration:** Benchmark selection (retailer vs. category) and KPI selection should be independently configurable, not tied to each other.<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
{*}Assumptions{*}:<br/>
<br/>
Phase 1 can be delivered as an enhancement to the existing Shopper Appeal report, without a report redesign.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
*Risks*<br/>
 <br/>
 - Types 2 and 3 carry real scope-creep risk once dimension nesting (geo, format, banner) is introduced; starting design work before Phase 1 ships could distract from the PI4 commitment.<br/>
—<br/>
 
  </td>
