</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Once several campaigns have been measured, the results become inputs to the next campaign rather than a record of the last one.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Measurement that only describes the past leaves the planning decision unchanged. The commercial position shifts substantially when the measurement layer becomes the thing planning depends on.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Turn accumulated measured results into guidance: which audiences respond, how much advertising is worth buying, and how large a holdout a given campaign needs.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Moves the product from reporting to advising, which is a different position in the value chain<br/>
* Improves the return on every subsequent campaign<br/>
* Quantifies exactly how small a control group can be, which strengthens the conversation with the partner<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* The relationship between how often shoppers are reached and the effect produced<br/>
* The point beyond which additional advertising produces no detectable effect<br/>
* A forecast for a proposed campaign, with its uncertainty, and a refusal where history is too thin<br/>
* Guidance on where additional budget produces the most incremental return<br/>
* The minimum holdout needed to detect an effect of a given size<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Automated budget allocation or campaign execution<br/>
* Any recommendation presented without its uncertainty<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* A forecast refuses rather than guessing where history is insufficient<br/>
* Every recommendation carries its uncertainty<br/>
* The holdout calculation is reproducible and documented<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Guidance used in planning at least one campaign<br/>
* Demonstrable improvement in incremental return on campaigns planned with it<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Several campaigns measured under incremental effect measurement
  </td>
