                <tr id="issuerow9995338" rel="9995338" data-issuekey="CR-40905" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    NIQ Activate
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CR-40905" href="https://adlm.nielseniq.com/jira/browse/CR-40905">CR-40905</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Mo Placeholder - Decomposition of the incremental result
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype">    Epic
</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                <span class=" jira-issue-status-lozenge aui-lozenge jira-issue-status-lozenge-default jira-issue-status-lozenge-new aui-lozenge-subtle jira-issue-status-lozenge-max-width-medium" data-tooltip="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" title="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" tabindex="0">Draft</span>    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">           High
    </td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Lift on a promoted product is not the same as value to the retailer. Sales may have moved from a neighbouring product, or been brought forward from next month.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
A brand that lifts its own product by taking sales from the one beside it has generated nothing for the retailer, and the current figures cannot tell the difference. This is the question a sophisticated buyer asks second.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Explain where incremental sales came from: taken from neighbouring products, gained across the brand, brought forward in time, and what remains as genuine category growth.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Answers the retailer&#39;s question rather than only the advertiser&#39;s<br/>
* Protects the category from campaigns that appear to work and do not<br/>
* Differentiates the product from anything an advertising network can offer<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* Estimation of sales taken from neighbouring products<br/>
* Estimation of gains across the rest of the brand<br/>
* Estimation of purchases brought forward rather than added<br/>
* A combined view showing how the incremental figure resolves into net category effect<br/>
* Observation extending beyond the campaign window, far enough to see purchases brought forward<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Publishing any component on its own, which is misleading without the others<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* The components reconcile to the net effect<br/>
* Reporting extends past the measurement window far enough to observe acceleration<br/>
* The assumptions behind the baseline are stated<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Decomposition reproduced on two campaigns with its error characterised<br/>
* Used in at least one category-level conversation with the retailer<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Incremental effect measurement<br/>
# A decision on whether the existing promotional baseline method can be reused, which would substantially reduce this work
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    phase-3, retail-media</td>
                                            <td class="customfield_35023"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_31204"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_14941"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_43010"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_25303"></td>
