                <tr id="issuerow9995337" rel="9995337" data-issuekey="CR-40904" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    NIQ Activate
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CR-40904" href="https://adlm.nielseniq.com/jira/browse/CR-40904">CR-40904</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Mo Placeholder - Modelled measurement where no control exists
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype">    Epic
</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                <span class=" jira-issue-status-lozenge aui-lozenge jira-issue-status-lozenge-default jira-issue-status-lozenge-new aui-lozenge-subtle jira-issue-status-lozenge-max-width-medium" data-tooltip="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" title="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" tabindex="0">Draft</span>    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">           High
    </td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Some campaigns will run without a control group, and some channels can never provide one because they return no shopper-level exposure.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
The choice is between reporting nothing for those campaigns and reporting an estimate. An estimate is useful if it is honestly labelled and dangerous if it is not.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Produce a modelled estimate where no control existed, presented so that it can never be mistaken for a measured result.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Extends coverage to campaigns and channels that would otherwise be unreportable<br/>
* Keeps the distinction between measured and modelled visible, protecting the measured figures<br/>
* Gives a defensible answer where the alternative is silence or a bad comparison<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* An estimate produced by comparing exposed shoppers to comparable unexposed shoppers<br/>
* Published diagnostics showing how comparable the two groups actually were<br/>
* A store-level comparison where shoppers cannot be identified at all<br/>
* Distinct presentation, carried through every screen and every export<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Presenting a modelled estimate as measured effect, in any circumstance<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* A modelled figure cannot be mistaken for a measured one in any view or export<br/>
* Diagnostics are published alongside every modelled estimate<br/>
* The assumptions behind the estimate are stated wherever it appears<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Campaigns without a control are reported rather than omitted<br/>
* No modelled figure quoted as a measured result<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Measurement dataset<br/>
# Reason codes for non-exposure, if available
