                <tr id="issuerow9995336" rel="9995336" data-issuekey="CR-40903" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    NIQ Activate
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CR-40903" href="https://adlm.nielseniq.com/jira/browse/CR-40903">CR-40903</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Mo Placeholder - Effect reporting
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype">    Epic
</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                <span class=" jira-issue-status-lozenge aui-lozenge jira-issue-status-lozenge-default jira-issue-status-lozenge-new aui-lozenge-subtle jira-issue-status-lozenge-max-width-medium" data-tooltip="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" title="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" tabindex="0">Draft</span>    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">           High
    </td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Incremental results are the most consequential and most misread figures in the product. How they are presented determines whether they are understood or over-read.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Published research is consistent that readers misinterpret every common presentation of uncertainty. A result presented conventionally will be read as more certain than it is, and an inconclusive result will be read as a weak positive.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Present incremental effect so that a non-technical reader correctly distinguishes a conclusive result from an inconclusive one, without being told which is which.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Protects every other figure in the product: one over-claimed result damages all of them<br/>
* Makes the strongest commercial figure usable by people who are not analysts<br/>
* Removes the need for a caveat conversation alongside every report<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* A new effect page showing the estimate, its uncertainty, whether it is conclusive, and the smallest effect the campaign could have detected<br/>
* A breakdown page showing effect by audience, by frequency and by placement, with uncertainty on each, so that overlapping results are visible rather than implied by ranking<br/>
* Extension of the reconciliation view to include the incremental step<br/>
* Period-over-period comparison, now permissible because it sits alongside a control group<br/>
* An inconclusive result presented as a stated verdict rather than as a small figure<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Modelled estimates, which are presented differently and arrive later<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* A non-technical reader correctly separates a conclusive result from an inconclusive one in testing<br/>
* Overlap between audiences is visible rather than implied by their order<br/>
* An inconclusive result cannot be read as a positive one anywhere on the page or in an export<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Comprehension tested with real advertisers and passing<br/>
* No instance of an inconclusive result being reported as an effect<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Incremental effect measurement<br/>
# Research on how the uncertainty display is read
