                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Everything in phase one describes what happened. Whether the campaign caused it requires comparing exposed shoppers to a group deliberately held back at random.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Without incremental measurement the product reports the same class of figures as the media partner, and competes on their ground. Incremental margin against a held-out control is the figure no advertising network can produce.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Compute incremental purchasers, sales, units, margin and return, each with a confidence interval and a statement of whether the result is conclusive.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* The figure that justifies a price and wins a renewal conversation<br/>
* Advertiser analytics teams can verify the method, which no competitor currently allows<br/>
* Wasted spend becomes identifiable rather than assumed<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* Incremental purchasers, sales, units, margin, return on spend and profit return<br/>
* A confidence interval on every effect figure<br/>
* A statement of whether a result is conclusive, and if not, the smallest effect the campaign could have detected<br/>
* Effect broken down by audience, by how often shoppers were reached, and by placement<br/>
* Our figure computed on both our window and the partner&#39;s, so the effect of the window is visible<br/>
* A step-by-step explanation of the gap between the partner&#39;s figure and ours<br/>
* Verification that a known effect is recovered and that a null result stays null<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Any modelling. This epic is arithmetic against a control group<br/>
* Explaining where incremental sales came from, which is decomposition and comes later<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* A planted effect is recovered and a null result stays null<br/>
* Every effect figure carries an interval and a statement of whether it is conclusive<br/>
* An underpowered campaign reports as not conclusive and cannot be read as a small effect<br/>
* Effect by audience is available wherever the audience identifier returned<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Three campaigns measured end to end with balance checks passing<br/>
* Incremental figures used in at least one renewal conversation<br/>
* No effect figure published without its interval<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Test and control assignment, and the agreed mechanism<br/>
# The audience identifier returned on exposure, for the audience breakdown<br/>
# A written definition of what is being estimated, agreed with data science
  </td>
