                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Results leave the product. They are printed, pasted into decks, and sent to advertisers, often by someone who did not produce them.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
A figure that loses its qualifier on the way out is a figure that will be quoted without it. Once that happens the product cannot control what is claimed on its behalf.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Make every exported artefact carry what qualifies its figures, and make an advertiser-facing view that is generated rather than hand-assembled.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Protects the product&#39;s credibility outside its own screens<br/>
* Removes the manual step of preparing an advertiser report, and the errors that come with it<br/>
* Ensures what an advertiser receives is defensible by construction<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* A printable result view<br/>
* A data export carrying method, window, population, currency date and every qualifier<br/>
* An advertiser-facing view containing only figures that can be defended, generated automatically<br/>
* Refusal to produce an export that would lose a qualifier, stating what is missing<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Scheduled distribution or email delivery<br/>
* Advertiser access to the product itself, if that is decided separately<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* No export can lose an interval or a method label<br/>
* The advertiser view requires no manual editing before it is sent<br/>
* An export that would drop a qualifier fails and says why<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Advertiser reports produced without manual assembly<br/>
* No instance of an exported figure being quoted without its qualifier<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Campaign result reporting
  </td>
