                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
The quality floors decide daily whether figures can be published. Someone has to be able to see that at a glance, before an advertiser does.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Without a monitoring surface, a quality breach is discovered as a missing or wrong figure downstream, usually by the person least equipped to diagnose it.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Give operations one page answering whether today&#39;s numbers can be published, and if not, why.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Problems are caught internally rather than externally<br/>
* Reduces time to diagnose a reporting issue from days to minutes<br/>
* Trend degradation is visible before it becomes a breach<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* A new data health page showing each quality measure against its floor over time<br/>
* What is currently withheld, why, and which campaigns are affected<br/>
* Feed status and how current each is<br/>
* Breach history<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Fixing the underlying data quality issues<br/>
* Alerting configuration, which belongs to operations tooling<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* Every operational measure in the phase one catalogue appears here or, for measurability, on the campaign list<br/>
* An operator can answer whether today is publishable from one page<br/>
* A breach is visible here before it appears as a missing figure elsewhere<br/>
* Every current suppression is listed with its cause<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Quality issues detected internally before any external report is affected<br/>
* Mean time to diagnose a reporting issue measurably reduced<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Data quality floors and figure suppression
  </td>
