                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Every figure in this product will at some point be challenged, usually by someone who was not in the room when it was produced.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
A figure that cannot be traced to its basis cannot be defended, and in practice will not be believed. Provenance added later is never complete.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Make the basis of any number reachable in one action, from anywhere it appears.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Any figure can be defended on the spot rather than after an investigation<br/>
* Reduces the analyst time spent reconstructing how a number was produced<br/>
* Makes internal review of a new measure possible without reading code<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* A panel, opened from any figure, giving its definition, how it was calculated, the campaign and population behind it, the window applied, the data it was computed from, and how to reproduce it<br/>
* Reachable from every figure on every page, without losing the reader&#39;s place<br/>
* A figure that cannot produce this does not display<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Exposing underlying shopper-level records<br/>
* A general query or exploration tool<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* Every figure in the product opens its basis in one action<br/>
* The panel states the method, the window and the date the data was current<br/>
* A figure with no available basis is not rendered<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Challenges to figures are resolved within the conversation<br/>
* No published figure lacks a retrievable basis<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Measure library
