                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
The media partner reports its own attributed result on its own window and model. Ours will differ, and an advertiser will see both.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Two credible organisations reporting different numbers for the same campaign, with no explanation of why, damages trust in both. The difference is expected and explainable, but only if it is explained deliberately.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Show both figures side by side and explain the difference, in terms an advertiser can repeat to their own team.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Removes the most common objection in a retail media conversation before it is raised<br/>
* Positions us as explaining rather than correcting, which protects the partner relationship<br/>
* Turns a discrepancy into evidence of rigour<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* A new reconciliation page showing both figures, each labelled with the method and window that produced it<br/>
* A step-by-step view of the difference, naming each cause: different window, different attribution basis, and later, incrementality<br/>
* A check of the partner&#39;s attributed sales against transactions for the same products and period<br/>
* A plain-language explanation generated from the components rather than written by hand<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Adjusting either figure to agree with the other<br/>
* Any presentation that frames the partner&#39;s figure as incorrect<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* Every partner-reported measure in the phase one catalogue appears here or on the result page, under the partner&#39;s name and window<br/>
* A reader can state why the two numbers differ without asking anyone<br/>
* The page reads as an explanation and never as a correction<br/>
* Both figures retain their own method and window wherever they appear<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* The reconciliation view is used in advertiser conversations<br/>
* Attribution differences stop being raised as data quality incidents<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Measure library<br/>
# Ingestion of partner attributed results
  </td>
