                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Beneath the headline result sit two questions: how the advertising was delivered and what it cost, and what exposed shoppers went on to buy.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Without these, the result screen is a set of figures nobody can interrogate, and every follow-up question becomes an analyst request.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Deliver two detail pages that answer the delivery and outcome questions without support.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Follow-up questions are answered in the product rather than by a person<br/>
* Poor delivery is distinguishable from poor response, which are different problems with different owners<br/>
* Spend that carries no measurable return becomes visible rather than assumed<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* A new delivery page carrying every delivery, reach, frequency and spend-efficiency measure in the phase one catalogue: pacing against the flight, shoppers reached against the audience published, how often they were reached, the spread of that frequency, where the advertising ran, and what each placement cost per thousand, per click and per shopper reached<br/>
* A new outcome page carrying every purchase, commercial and behaviour measure in the phase one catalogue: how many exposed shoppers bought, at what rate, what they bought, what it was worth, what margin it carried, margin against media cost, basket value, units per buyer, how quickly purchases followed exposure, and how many buyers were new to the brand<br/>
* A standing statement on the outcome page that these figures describe what happened and do not establish what the campaign caused<br/>
* A statement per campaign of which channels it ran on and what can be reported for each<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Any comparison between exposed shoppers and shoppers who were not exposed, in any form<br/>
* Effect figures, which require a control group<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* Every delivery, spend, outcome and behaviour measure in the phase one catalogue appears on one of these two pages<br/>
* Every figure carries its method label<br/>
* The outcome page states its own limits without the reader having to know them<br/>
* No route exists, through any filter or export, to compare exposed against unexposed shoppers<br/>
* Channels with no measurable return are shown as such rather than omitted<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* A measurable drop in support requests for delivery and outcome questions<br/>
* Channels carrying spend with no return are identified and acted on<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Measure library<br/>
# Campaign result reporting
  </td>
