                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
No reporting surface exists for retail media measurement. The result of a campaign is the artefact an advertiser sees, usually in a meeting, usually while being challenged.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Without a reporting surface there is no product. And a surface that presents figures without their method and uncertainty produces confident readings of numbers that do not support them, which is worse than no reporting at all.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Deliver the two screens an advertiser conversation runs on: a list of campaigns showing what can be said about each, and a result screen for one campaign.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* The commercial artefact of the product, and the reason an advertiser renews<br/>
* Results become self-service rather than assembled by an analyst per request<br/>
* Every figure shown carries what qualifies it, so nothing can be quoted out of context<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* A new campaign list page: filterable and sortable, showing for each campaign its advertiser, flight, spend, shoppers reached, and what can honestly be reported about it<br/>
* A new campaign result page carrying: a plain-language statement of what the campaign did; the headline figures for shoppers reached, spend, purchase outcome and commercial outcome; a profit view showing margin generated against media cost; summaries of delivery and of the comparison with the partner&#39;s own figure<br/>
* Each figure labelled with how it was produced, so a counted figure is visibly different from an estimated one<br/>
* A fixed statement of basis on every result page: method, window, population and the date the data was current<br/>
* Printing to a single page without losing any label, interval or basis<br/>
* Loading, empty, error and withheld states on both pages<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Any figure requiring a control group, which arrives in a later epic<br/>
* Cross-campaign aggregation, which would combine figures produced by different methods<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* A reader seeing only the opening statement and the headline figures states correctly what the campaign achieved<br/>
* Measurability is visible in the list without opening a campaign<br/>
* Printing preserves every label and qualifier<br/>
* No figure renders without its method label<br/>
* Where a figure is withheld, the reason appears in its place rather than a blank or a zero<br/>
* Every phase one measure in the agreed catalogue has a home on a screen. A measure that is computed and never displayed is treated as an incomplete epic, not as a future enhancement<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* An advertiser conversation runs from this screen without a supporting spreadsheet<br/>
* Time from campaign end to a shareable result drops to the stated reporting window<br/>
* No incident in which a figure was quoted without its qualifier<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Measure library and quality floors<br/>
# Access to the design system
