                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Roughly thirty-four measures are needed before any modelling: delivery, reach, frequency, spend efficiency, purchase outcomes, commercial outcomes and the partner&#39;s own reported figures.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Measures defined in reports rather than in one place drift apart. Two teams compute the same metric differently, both believe they are right, and the discrepancy surfaces in front of an advertiser.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Define every measure once, in one place, with its formula, grain and supported breakdowns, so that two people computing it independently obtain the same answer.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Figures agree across every screen and export because they come from one definition<br/>
* A measure can be changed in one place and every consumer follows<br/>
* A published figure can always state which version of a definition produced it<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* All phase one measures: delivery, reach, spend efficiency, purchase outcome, commercial outcome, partner-reported<br/>
* A registry recording each measure&#39;s formula, grain and supported breakdowns<br/>
* Breakdown by campaign, audience, banner, country, placement and product where the measure supports it<br/>
* Results stored with the definition version that produced them<br/>
* A test per measure that fails when the calculation is deliberately broken<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Any measure requiring a control group or a model<br/>
* Presentation of the measures<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* Every phase one measure in the agreed catalogue is computable and stored<br/>
* Each measure fails its test when the calculation is broken on purpose<br/>
* Results carry the definition version they were computed under<br/>
* Partner-reported figures are stored under the partner&#39;s name and window and are never recomputed<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* All catalogue measures available for every measurable campaign<br/>
* Two independent implementations of any measure agree<br/>
* No figure exists in the product that is not defined in the registry<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# The measurement dataset
