                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Exposure, assignment, transactions and margin currently live in four places. Every figure the product reports needs them joined.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Without a single joined dataset per campaign, every figure is computed by a different route, two people get different answers, and a past campaign cannot be re-measured to the same numbers.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Produce one record per shopper per campaign joining exposure, assignment, purchases and margin, frozen when the campaign is measured.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Every figure in the product derives from one place, so figures agree with each other by construction<br/>
* A past campaign re-measures identically, which is what makes a result defensible months later<br/>
* Adding a new measure becomes a small job rather than a new pipeline<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* One record per shopper per campaign, joining exposure, group assignment, purchases and margin<br/>
* Purchase outcomes computed over the campaign&#39;s product scope<br/>
* Basket outcomes computed over all products, kept separate from product outcomes<br/>
* Freezing at measurement time, with the freeze recorded<br/>
* A rebuild check proving a past campaign reproduces exactly<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* The measures themselves, which are a separate epic<br/>
* Any reporting surface<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* One record exists per shopper per campaign for a completed campaign<br/>
* A campaign rebuilt from frozen inputs produces identical numbers<br/>
* Product outcomes and basket outcomes are separately computed and separately labelled<br/>
* The dataset carries country, banner and audience so results can be cut by them<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Rebuild of any past campaign matches the original exactly<br/>
* Build completes within the nightly window at production volume<br/>
* Every published figure traces to this dataset<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Ingestion, identity resolution, product scope and export extension all in place
  </td>
