                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
To say a campaign caused something, a comparable group of people must not have seen it, chosen at random before the campaign runs. Two routes are possible: we withhold the control from the export, or the partner withholds it at serve time and returns the list.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
No mechanism exists today, and the decision cannot be applied retrospectively. Every campaign that runs without an assignment recorded before exposure is permanently descriptive, no matter what is built afterwards.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Record a randomised test and control assignment for every campaign, before first exposure, reproducibly, whichever route is agreed.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* The single dependency that makes causal measurement possible at all<br/>
* Campaigns running now become measurable later rather than being lost<br/>
* Assignment can be shown to be sound when an advertiser&#39;s analysts examine it<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* Storage of assignment per shopper per campaign, with the seed and method used<br/>
* Randomisation implemented separately from any targeting or optimisation logic<br/>
* A balance check across groups, computed and stored per campaign<br/>
* Reproduction of any past assignment from its stored seed<br/>
* Detection of a person assigned to opposing groups across audiences in the same period<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* The choice of mechanism itself, which is a commercial and partner decision<br/>
* Any use of the assignment in reporting, which is a later epic<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* An assignment reproduces exactly from its stored seed<br/>
* Assignment timestamps prove the decision preceded first exposure<br/>
* A balance report is produced and stored for every campaign<br/>
* A deliberately biased assignment is detected by the balance check<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Every campaign after go-live has an assignment recorded before exposure<br/>
* Balance checks pass on the agreed attributes<br/>
* Any past campaign&#39;s assignment can be regenerated on demand<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Agreement on which of the two control routes is used<br/>
# Single-person view, in multi-banner countries, so assignment is made on the person
  </td>
