                <tr id="issuerow9995318" rel="9995318" data-issuekey="CR-40890" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    NIQ Activate
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CR-40890" href="https://adlm.nielseniq.com/jira/browse/CR-40890">CR-40890</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Mo Placeholder - Audience export extension for measurement
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype">    Epic
</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                <span class=" jira-issue-status-lozenge aui-lozenge jira-issue-status-lozenge-default jira-issue-status-lozenge-new aui-lozenge-subtle jira-issue-status-lozenge-max-width-medium" data-tooltip="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" title="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" tabindex="0">Draft</span>    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">           High
    </td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> 11/Sep/2026 1:59 PM </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 26/Aug/2026 3:59 PM </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Audiences are already exported to the partner. Measurement needs three additions to every exported row so that exposure can later be traced back to the audience a shopper came from.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Exposure data returns without the audience identifier, so exposed shoppers cannot be connected to the audience they originated from. Incrementality by audience is impossible, and so is comparing an exposed group to the right control.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Carry the audience identifier, banner and country on every exported shopper row, and record the export so returns can be reconciled against it.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Results become answerable by audience rather than only by campaign<br/>
* Reach and results can be reported by banner and country where those matter<br/>
* Discrepancies between what we sent and what came back become detectable<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* Audience identifier on every exported shopper row, across all export types<br/>
* Banner and country columns where required<br/>
* A record of every export with its row count, for reconciliation<br/>
* A control flag on the export, if the agreed control mechanism requires one<br/>
* Membership retained as exported, so what was targeted is recoverable later<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Changing how audiences are defined or selected<br/>
* Any change to the maximum number of shoppers an export may contain<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* Every exported row carries its audience identifier<br/>
* The maximum exportable record count is unchanged from before the additional columns<br/>
* Export row counts are recorded and comparable to what returns<br/>
* Membership as exported is recoverable for any past export<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Audience identifier present on one hundred per cent of exported rows<br/>
* Export and return counts reconcile exactly for four consecutive weeks<br/>
* At least one campaign reports results broken down by audience<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Whether country is required, and for which countries<br/>
# One agreed name for the banner attribute, which is currently named two ways<br/>
# The control mechanism decision, if a control flag is to be included<br/>
# The partner returning the audience identifier on exposure, which is a separate agreement
  </td>
