                <tr id="issuerow9995317" rel="9995317" data-issuekey="CR-40889" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    NIQ Activate
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CR-40889" href="https://adlm.nielseniq.com/jira/browse/CR-40889">CR-40889</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Mo Placeholder - Product mapping and campaign product scope
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype">    Epic
</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                <span class=" jira-issue-status-lozenge aui-lozenge jira-issue-status-lozenge-default jira-issue-status-lozenge-new aui-lozenge-subtle jira-issue-status-lozenge-max-width-medium" data-tooltip="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" title="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" tabindex="0">Draft</span>    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">           High
    </td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Mohammad Belghiszadeh
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> 11/Sep/2026 1:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Aug/2026 8:58 PM </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
A campaign promotes a set of products. To say whether shoppers bought those products, we need to know which they were, and we need the partner&#39;s product codes to map to ours.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
Neither the campaign&#39;s product scope nor the mapping between product coding systems is specified on either side today. Without both, no outcome measure has anything to compute over, and the gap is invisible until the first campaign is measured.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Establish, for every campaign, the set of our own product codes it promoted, and publish the match rate of the mapping that produced it.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Sales, units and margin can be attributed to the products a campaign actually promoted<br/>
* A campaign whose scope cannot be established is identified before it is reported on, rather than after<br/>
* The commercial figures that differentiate this product become computable at all<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* Ingestion or derivation of each campaign&#39;s product scope<br/>
* A mapping between the partner&#39;s product codes and ours, with a published match rate<br/>
* Per-campaign reporting of unmapped products, so scope gaps are visible<br/>
* A campaign with no usable product scope is marked unmeasurable rather than measured against everything<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Reconciling the partner&#39;s product hierarchy with ours beyond what the mapping requires<br/>
* Product data quality work in the source catalogue<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* A campaign resolves to a list of our product codes<br/>
* The product match rate is published with its floor<br/>
* A campaign with no usable scope is labelled unmeasurable and produces no outcome figure<br/>
* Unmapped products are listed per campaign rather than silently excluded<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Product match rate at or above the agreed floor across live campaigns<br/>
* Every measured campaign has a stated product scope<br/>
* No campaign produces a sales figure without a resolved product set<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# How campaign product scope is received from the partner � not specified today<br/>
# How product codes map between the two sides � not specified today<br/>
# These two questions are the largest source of estimating uncertainty in the whole programme
  </td>
