                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
We hold and export the loyalty identifier. The partner&#39;s platform resolves it to their own shopper identifier, and exposure returns keyed on theirs. Every measurement depends on joining the two back together.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Problem / opportunity<br/>
If exposure cannot be resolved back to our own shopper identity, nothing can be joined to transactions and no shopper-level measurement of any kind is possible. Identity quality is also inherited rather than controlled, which makes it a monitoring obligation rather than a one-off check.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Resolve returned exposure to our loyalty identifier on ingestion, and publish the match rate as a daily measure from the first day.<br/>
<br/>
h3. Business outcome / value<br/>
* Every downstream figure is keyed on an identity we own and control<br/>
* Degradation in match quality is visible immediately rather than discovered as unexplained figures<br/>
* A clear, defensible answer exists to the question of how much of the audience we can actually measure<br/>
<br/>
h3. In scope<br/>
* Resolution applied during ingestion, so exposure carries our shopper identity<br/>
* A daily identity match rate with a defined floor and an alert when breached<br/>
* Unresolved identifiers retained and counted rather than discarded, so losses are visible<br/>
* Match rate available per feed and per campaign<br/>
<br/>
h3. Out of scope<br/>
* Changing how the partner resolves identity. Their resolution is theirs and we inherit its quality<br/>
* Any attempt to re-identify a shopper from partner data<br/>
<br/>
h3. Acceptance criteria<br/>
* Exposure records resolve to our shopper identity at or above the agreed floor<br/>
* Unresolved rows are counted and retained, never silently dropped<br/>
* The match rate is published daily before any reporting screen exists<br/>
* A simulated drop in match quality raises an alert the same day<br/>
<br/>
h3. Measure of success<br/>
* Match rate published every day with no gaps<br/>
* Match rate at or above the agreed floor for four consecutive weeks<br/>
* Every campaign report can state what share of its audience was matchable<br/>
<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
# Confirmation of which identifier we export and which the partner returns<br/>
# The partner returning the mapping, or exposure carrying our identifier directly
