                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CR-39951                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
<br/>
MediaRithmics is the CDP used by Unlimitail. we are going to need to push to it shopper segments in a scheduled/automated way using our automation capabilities. <br/>
The structure of the exported file will go through some changes as specified in other epics (see dependencies).<br/>
<br/>
The main changes specified on other epics:<br/>
1) Add segment ID to the automated export file <br/>
2) Add shopper banner field to the exported file (brazil portal only)<br/>
3) Add control group Y/N to the exported file<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
 * Provide Easy and granular targeting capabilities for the Unlimitail team<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h2. In scope<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
 * Build the integration with the CDP in the agreed format and destination.<br/>
 * Scheduled export should be supported (existing)<br/>
 * User can still export one off segment without waiting for the schedule and it&#39;ll be pushed to the CDP<br/>
 * The default exported file structure should include some changes specified in other epics (Suggested slicing not confirmed with the customer):<br/>
 ** Phase 1: Export loyalty IDs only (Existing)<br/>
 ** Phase 2: Add segment ID to all 3 unlimitail portals (CR-39951)  + banner to brazil portal (CR-39948)<br/>
 ** Phase 3: Add control group yes/no column (CR-39945)<br/>
 * Everything in this epic is related to the automated export not to the manual XLS/CSV export (see other epics to address this).<br/>
<br/>
h2. Out of Scope<br/>
 * N/A<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h2. Acceptance Criteria<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
 * Integration with the CDP is implemented for automated segment exports.<br/>
 * Exported file is according to agreed format and to an agreed storage location.<br/>
 * Users can trigger a one-off segment export at any time without waiting for the next scheduled export and it will be pushed to the CDP.<br/>
 * Automated exports generate files using the agreed export structure.<br/>
 ** *Phase 1:* Automated exports include Loyalty ID only (current behavior).<br/>
 ** *Phase 2:* Automated exports include:<br/>
 *** Segment ID for all three Unlimitail portals (CR-39951).<br/>
 *** Banner field for the Brazil portal (CR-39948).<br/>
 ** *Phase 3:* Automated exports include a Control Group column with values *Yes* or *No* (CR-39945).<br/>
 * All changes delivered in this epic apply only to {*}automated exports{*}.<br/>
 * Any enhancements to manual XLS/CSV exports are out of scope for this epic and are delivered through separate pics<br/>
 <br/>
 * <br/>
----<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
<br/>
 # Unlimitail CDP (Mediarithmics) ingestion specifications (Including the name of the files not only structure)<br/>
 # Exported file naming<br/>
 # Storage address<br/>
 # Cadence of exports<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
----<br/>
h2. Mock-up / Figma<br/>
<br/>
N/A<br/>
<br/>
CC: [~bemo0001]  [~gene3001] <br/>
<br/>
 
