                <tr id="issuerow9921652" rel="9921652" data-issuekey="CR-39951" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    NIQ Activate
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CR-39951" href="https://adlm.nielseniq.com/jira/browse/CR-39951">CR-39951</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Placeholder - Unlimitail - export segment ID as part of segments &amp; audiences builder
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype">    Epic
</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                <span class=" jira-issue-status-lozenge aui-lozenge jira-issue-status-lozenge-default jira-issue-status-lozenge-new aui-lozenge-subtle jira-issue-status-lozenge-max-width-medium" data-tooltip="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" title="&lt;span class=&quot;jira-issue-status-tooltip-title&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;" tabindex="0">Draft</span>    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">           High
    </td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Tal Martsiano Shkedi
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Neta Gefen-Shternberg
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Eran Center
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 05/Aug/2026 6:25 AM </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 09/Sep/2026 9:57 AM </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CR-39948,                                                CR-39954,                                                CR-41564                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
Retail Media closed-loop measurement capabilities rely on linking audience segmentation data with campaign execution and shopper exposure data. To accurately measure campaign performance and calculate incrementality, segment membership must be maintained throughout the activation lifecycle and be available during the measurement phase.<br/>
h3. Problem / Opportunity<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Today, shopper exposure data received from media partners does not contain the segment identifier originally used during audience activation. As a result, Activate &amp; Unlimitail cannot reliably connect campaign-exposed shoppers back to the specific segment from which they originated. This limits the ability to perform incrementality analysis and compare exposed shoppers against the appropriate control group during closed-loop measurement.<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
Enable end-to-end traceability of audience segments throughout campaign activation and measurement by exporting the Activate segment ID with audience deliveries and ensuring it is returned as part of shopper exposure data (seperate epic). This will allow exposures to be associated with the originating segment and support accurate incrementality and control-group analysis.<br/>
----<br/>
h2. Business Outcome / Value<br/>
h3. Expected Benefits<br/>
 * Enable accurate linkage between audience segments and shopper exposure data throughout the campaign lifecycle.<br/>
 * Support incrementality measurement by allowing exposed shoppers to be associated with their originating segment and corresponding control group.<br/>
 * Measure the effectiveness of campaigns non walled garden campaigns in a precise way<br/>
<br/>
h2. In scope<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
 * Export the segment ID with every shopper segment delivery/export<br/>
 ** Including manual shopper ID export<br/>
 ** Shopper Insights data export<br/>
 ** Automatic exports (scheduled or manual)<br/>
 * Column Name: Activate Segment ID <br/>
 * Ensure the segment ID is associated with each shopper record included in the export.<br/>
 * This change should apply only for Unlimitail for now and can be enabled upon request to other customers (should not change existing export structure for other customers).<br/>
 * Number of allowed exportable shoppers should not decrease vs. current status by adding this new column<br/>
<br/>
h2. Out of Scope<br/>
 * Deployment of this change to all customers<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h2. Acceptance Criteria<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
<br/>
 * The export includes a new column named *&quot;Activate Segment ID&quot;* in all shopper segment exports for *Unlimitail* portals (no change to other portals)<br/>
 * The *&quot;Activate Segment ID&quot;* column is populated with the corresponding segment ID for every shopper record included in the export.<br/>
 * The new column is included in the following export types:<br/>
 ** Manual Shopper ID exports<br/>
 ** Shopper Insights data exports<br/>
 ** Automatic exports (scheduled and manually triggered)<br/>
 * The exported segment ID accurately represents the segment from which the shopper record was exported.<br/>
 * Existing export formats and schemas for *non-Unlimitail customers* remain unchanged by default.<br/>
 * The capability can be enabled for additional customers through configuration without requiring code changes to the export logic.<br/>
 * Adding the *&quot;Activate Segment ID&quot;* column does not reduce the maximum number of shopper records that can be exported compared to the current implementation. # <br/>
----<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
<br/>
 # Unlimitail CDP (Mediarithmics) ingestion specifications.<br/>
 # Agree on how we receive the segment ID back from Unlimitail<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
----<br/>
h2. Mock-up / Figma<br/>
<br/>
N/A<br/>
<br/>
CC: [~bemo0001]  [~gene3001] <br/>
