                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
<br/>
Unlimitail leverages retailer shopper audiences to power media activation and campaign measurement. As part of its Carrefour partnership, Unlimitail is onboarding shopper data from France, Spain, and Brazil. Each country maintains its own shopper identity ecosystem, with shopper IDs being unique and managed independently at the country level.<br/>
<br/>
This epic is about handling some challenges that arise from the above in the segments and audiences builder.<br/>
h3. Problem / Opportunity<br/>
<br/>
Unlimitail activates and measures media campaigns using retailer shopper audiences across Carrefour markets, beginning with France, Spain, and Brazil. While shopper identities are managed at the country level, Brazil presents a unique challenge: Carrefour Brazil consists of three distinct banners (sub-retailers), each maintaining its own shopper identifier system.<br/>
<br/>
As a result, a single shopper who transacts across multiple banners can be represented by multiple shopper IDs. Since all Brazilian banners are managed within a single Unlimitail portal, Unlimitail requires a mechanism to:<br/>
 # Distinguish shoppers by banner affiliation.<br/>
 # Identify the banner associated with each shopper ID.<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
<br/>
Provide a way for Unlimitail to target shoppers by banner and measure results by banner in Carrefour Brazil<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
----<br/>
h2. Business Outcome / Value<br/>
h3. Expected Benefits<br/>
 * Allowing Unlimitail to Target &amp; measure at carrefour banner level (which is mandatory for them)<br/>
<br/>
h2. In scope<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
 *  For the brazil portal (only) add a shopper attribute named: Shopper Banner<br/>
 ** It should classify shoppers into their respective banners banners <br/>
 * In the automatic export as well as the manual export add a column named Banner which will export the shoppers Banner ID/Banner Name (TBD)<br/>
 ** This relates to BR portal only, not required for France or Spain<br/>
 * For the manual exports this relates to both types (shopper IDs only and Shopper Insights data)<br/>
 * Should not impact any other existing client environments (including other unlimitail environements)<br/>
<br/>
h3. Non- Functional<br/>
 * Current export limitations of number of shopper should be maintained even after the enhacement.<br/>
<br/>
h2. Out of Scope<br/>
 * Managing control assignment dependencies across different segments<br/>
----<br/>
h2. Acceptance Criteria<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
<br/>
 # Shopper banner attribute is added to the BR portal<br/>
 # Shopper banner column is added to the automated exported files (ID/Name TBD)<br/>
 # Shopper banner column is added to the manual exports (IDs only or shopper insights data)<br/>
 # No change to the exports in other customer environments (including Unlimitail)<br/>
<br/>
 # <br/>
----<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
<br/>
 # Unlimitail CDP (Mediarithmics) ingestion specifications.<br/>
 # Understand if we need country as well for the measurement purposes<br/>
 # Do we need a similar thing in the rest of the countries<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
----<br/>
h2. Mock-up / Figma<br/>
<br/>
N/A<br/>
<br/>
CC: [~bemo0001]  [~gene3001] <br/>
<br/>
 
