                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h3. Context<br/>
<br/>
Unlimitail leverages retailer shopper audiences for media activation and measurement. As audience activation use cases expand across markets, the existing Segments &amp; Audiences Builder requires enhancements to support the retail media (and personalization) measurement processes<br/>
This epic is focusing on the automated exports (either ad-hoc or scheduled).<br/>
h3. Problem / Opportunity<br/>
<br/>
Today, audience exports do not split shoppers to test and control in order to support measurement needs for retail media (incrementality vs. control)<br/>
h3. Objective<br/>
<br/>
Enhance Activate&#39;s Segments &amp; Audiences Builder automated export capabilities to select control shoppers out of the exported control group. this will be used for measurement purposes (test vs. control incrementality).<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
----<br/>
h2. Business Outcome / Value<br/>
h3. Expected Benefits<br/>
 * Reduce manual audience preparation efforts for campaign activation.<br/>
 * Support controlled test vs. control methodologies required for campaign measurement.<br/>
<br/>
h2. In scope<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
 * When leveraging the +automatic export capability+ (scheduled/ad-hoc) as part of an integration with an external system enable the capability to assign some shoppers to a control group - this is a generic capability<br/>
 * The control group selected should meet the statistical requirements (defined by DS) to represent the test group (in terms of the quality of selected shoppers). Can use similar approach to the offer control.<br/>
 * Non-deterministic approach: Re-exporting a segment might select a different group of shoppers as control.<br/>
 * Customers might request to support their own logic for control selection and we would need to be able to support custom logic ({color:#de350b}TBD{color}).<br/>
 * The shoppers assigned/not assigned to control should be marked in the exported file in a designated column (Control group Yes/No)<br/>
 * Retailers/retail media players can decide if they want us to export only the test shoppers or both test &amp; control shoppers as part of the export.<br/>
 * NIQ Activate should maintain in its data base which shopper is assigned for test and which one is assigned for control per segment ID. this will be used for measurement purposes.<br/>
 * This test/control functionality should not be enabled by default to all customers (needs to be permitted) so we&#39;ll not hard backward compatibility.<br/>
 * Control selection of a shopper in one segment does not impact its selection to control on other segment (each segment has its own control group)<br/>
 * {color:#de350b}UI changes in segmentation studio to show which shoppers were selected for test vs. control - TBD{color}<br/>
<br/>
h3. Non- Functional<br/>
 * Scalable execution for hundreds of segments<br/>
 * Backward compatibility for customers without the capability enabled<br/>
 * Extensible design for standard and custom logic for control selection<br/>
 * DB Persistent and traceable test/control assignment data<br/>
<br/>
h2. Out of Scope<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
 * Regular/manual Excel/CSV exports support<br/>
<br/>
h3. Non-Functional<br/>
 * Guaranteeing the same control group across re-exports<br/>
 * Managing control assignment dependencies across different segments<br/>
----<br/>
h2. Acceptance Criteria<br/>
h3. Functional<br/>
<br/>
 # *Automatic* scheduled and ad-hoc exports (not the manual Excel/CSV ones) can assign shoppers to test and control groups.<br/>
 # Control selection meets DS-defined statistical requirements.<br/>
 # Re-exporting a segment may result in a different control group.<br/>
 # Export files include a {{Control Group}} column with {{Yes}} or {{No}} values.<br/>
 # Retailers or retail media players can choose whether to export test shoppers only or both test and control shoppers.<br/>
 # NIQ Activate persists test/control assignment per shopper and Segment ID for measurement.<br/>
 # The capability is permission-based and disabled by default.<br/>
 # Control group assignment is independent per segment.<br/>
 # {color:#de350b}Segmentation Studio UI changes are TBD {color}<br/>
<br/>
h3. Non-Functional<br/>
 # The solution scales to automatic export flows involving hundreds of segments.<br/>
 # Existing customers without the capability enabled retain current export behavior (no control).<br/>
 # The design supports both standard and custom control selection logic.<br/>
 # Test/control assignment data is persistent, traceable, and usable for measurement.<br/>
----<br/>
h3. Dependencies and open issues<br/>
<br/>
 # Unlimitail CDP (Mediarithmics) ingestion specifications.<br/>
 # Final agreement on control group methodology between Activate and Unlimitail/Internal DS.<br/>
 # UI for showing who are the control shoppers<br/>
 # {color:#de350b}Support for custom control selected TBD{color}<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
----<br/>
h2. Mock-up / Figma<br/>
<br/>
TBD<br/>
<br/>
CC: [~bemo0001]  [~gene3001] <br/>
<br/>
 
