                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CR-35737                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      h2. *Background*<br/>
<br/>
Activate has several reports which use backend lookback period parameters to define shopper groups (e.g., New, Activated, Retained, Lapsing shoppers in the Loyalty Behavior report, or defining new shoppers in New Product Launch and Event Analyzer).<br/>
<br/>
Today, shopper groups are defined via backend parameters:<br/>
 * {{civalue.reports.loyalty.period.previous}}<br/>
 * {{civalue.reports.loyalty.period.before}}<br/>
<br/>
The logic is based on two consecutive time windows:<br/>
 * *Previous Period (2 months)* – the recent period before the selected period<br/>
 * *Period Before (2 months)* – the period immediately before the previous period<br/>
<br/>
Together, a 2/4 setup represents 4 months total history.<br/>
<br/>
These periods are:<br/>
 * Applied uniformly across all users within a retailer environment<br/>
 * Not exposed for user selection<br/>
 * Used in Loyalty Behavior, New Product Launch, and Event Analyzer reports (the latter two only use the &quot;period before&quot; parameter to define new shoppers)<br/>
<br/>
*!image-2026-06-28-16-24-52-441.png!*<br/>
----<br/>
h2. *Problem*<br/>
<br/>
The current static configuration creates several limitations:<br/>
 * Different product categories have varying sales cycles (e.g., FMCG vs. durables) and should not share the same period definitions<br/>
 * Short sales cycle products may require shorter lookback windows, while longer cycles (e.g., durables) may require up to 12 months<br/>
 * No self-serve capability for analysts — configuration is fixed and controlled by the support team<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h2. *Opportunity*<br/>
<br/>
Enable users to dynamically select the time-period configuration directly within the report UI, allowing more accurate and flexible analysis driven by business context.<br/>
----<br/>
h2. *Requirements*<br/>
h3. *User Configuration*<br/>
<br/>
Introduce user-level configurable period selection within:<br/>
 * *Loyalty Behavior*<br/>
<br/>
 * <br/>
 ** Options: 2/4, 3/6, 4/8, 6/12 months<br/>
 * *New Product Launch*<br/>
<br/>
 * <br/>
 ** Options: 2/4, 3/6, 4/8, 6/12 months<br/>
 ** Used to define new shoppers in:<br/>
 *** Pie chart<br/>
 *** New category shoppers card<br/>
 * *Event Analyzer*<br/>
<br/>
 * <br/>
 ** Options: 2/4, 3/6, 4/8, 6/12 months<br/>
 ** Used to define new shoppers in:<br/>
 *** Top bar chart<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *System Behavior*<br/>
 * The filter selection should impact relevant calculations in each report<br/>
 * Default selection should follow the existing retailer configuration<br/>
 * User selection should persist between sessions (browser-level)<br/>
<br/>
h2. *Business Outcome / Value*<br/>
h3. *Client Value*<br/>
 * Ability to tailor analysis to product lifecycle<br/>
 * Improved user experience through self-service capabilities<br/>
<br/>
h3. *NIQ / Product Value*<br/>
 * Increased customer satisfaction<br/>
 * Increased report engagement and adoption<br/>
<br/>
h3. *Operational Efficiency*<br/>
 * Elimination of manual backend configuration changes<br/>
<br/>
h2. *Acceptance Criteria*<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *Control through the UI*<br/>
 * A new period selector is available in the Loyalty Behavior report filter bar<br/>
 * User can select from:<br/>
 ** 2/4 months<br/>
 ** 3/6 months<br/>
 ** 4/8 months<br/>
 ** 6/12 months<br/>
 * Selector includes a tooltip explaining its functionality<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *Default Behavior*<br/>
 * If no user preference exists:<br/>
 ** System applies retailer-level default configuration<br/>
 ** Default is reflected in the selector<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *Persistence*<br/>
 * User selection is saved to browser local storage<br/>
 * Selection is automatically applied in future sessions<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *Calculation Logic*<br/>
 * KPI calculations (New, Activated, Retained, Lapsing) update based on:<br/>
 ** previous period = first parameter<br/>
 ** period before = cumulative historical period<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *View Coverage*<br/>
 * Selected configuration applies consistently across:<br/>
 ** Aggregated view<br/>
 ** Trended view<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *Backend Mapping*<br/>
 * Selected values map correctly to:<br/>
 ** {{civalue.reports.loyalty.period.previous}}<br/>
 ** {{civalue.reports.loyalty.period.before}}<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *KPI Tooltips*<br/>
 * KPI tooltips dynamically reflect selected period definitions<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *New Product Launch*<br/>
 * Selector available with options: 4, 6, 8, 12 months<br/>
 * Used to define new shoppers in:<br/>
 ** Pie chart<br/>
 ** New category shoppers card<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *Event Analyzer*<br/>
 * Selector available with options: 4, 6, 8, 12 months<br/>
 * Used to define new shoppers in:<br/>
 ** Top bar chart<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h3. *Report Independence*<br/>
 * Selection does NOT propagate across reports<br/>
 * Each report maintains its own selection<br/>
<br/>
h2. *In Scope*<br/>
 * UI control for predefined period selection<br/>
 * Integration with calculation logic<br/>
 * Persistence via browser storage<br/>
 * Application across all report views<br/>
 * Dynamic KPI tooltips<br/>
<br/>
----<br/>
h2. *Out of Scope*<br/>
 * Custom or arbitrary period selection<br/>
 * Cross-device persistence{*}{{*}}<br/>
<br/>
h2. *Mockup/Figma*<br/>
 * {color:#de350b}*Figma make:{color}* [Dropdown Selector Mockup – Figma Make|https://www.figma.com/make/J7iiTrDxiIxx4l8jIl1VXX/Dropdown-Selector-Mockup?code-node-id=0-6&amp;p=f&amp;t=cgitIH80AqEz6Xr3-0&amp;fullscreen=1]<br/>
 * *Figma: TBD*<br/>
<br/>
h2. *Open Issues*<br/>
 * Check if parameters are being used in additional reports <br/>
<br/>
{{ }}<br/>
 <br/>
 #  
